  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given, for an ammeter, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>Total current, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></math> be the shunt resistance, then&nbsp;according to the question circuit diagram is given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"\"><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>&#8214;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mfenced></math> hence have equal potential difference<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0014_4d54bc21b4a7.png\" style=\"width: 348px; height: 170px;\" /></p><p>where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p>"
